        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "installation",
      "text": "When the backup battery input is used, an external 3 A slow-blow fuse must be connected in series.",
      "severity": "caution",
      "sourceRefs": [
        {
          "sourceId": "axis-a1601-install",
          "locator": "p. 27"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "installation",
      "text": "Supervised inputs (door monitor and REX) use end-of-line resistors. The guide lists 1 kΩ, 2.2 kΩ, 4.7 kΩ and 10 kΩ as verified values and shows parallel (default) and serial connection diagrams — wire from those diagrams.",
      "severity": "info",
      "sourceRefs": [
        {
          "sourceId": "axis-a1601-install",
          "locator": "p. 22"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "installation",
      "text": "Inductive loads on configurable outputs (e.g. a relay) need a diode in parallel with the load to protect against voltage transients.",
